<%#
  The text board's posting form. `views/textboard.ejs` includes this name for its new-thread
  form, and a text board takes no uploads (`models/forms/makeThread.js` refuses a file on one),
  so it is the ordinary posting form with the attachment rows, the Tegaki button and the
  file rules left out - see `textBoard` in `partials/post-form.ejs`. The poll editor stays, and
  is shown rather than hidden behind the attachment-type selector that a text board has no use
  for.

  What marks the upload as optional is the <form> this is included in: it carries
  `data-requires-file="false"`, which is what `public/js/upload.js` reads before insisting on a
  file. (`#reply-form` is exempted there on its own, which is why the text thread's reply form
  needs nothing but the `textBoard` flag.)
%>
<%- include('post-form', { textBoard: true }) %>
